  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the Humanitarian Response to Crisis-Affected Populations in Countries Affected by the Ukraine Crisis</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The humanitarian community is currently projecting around 12 million people in need of assistance within Ukraine, of which 4.3 million would be internally displaced persons (IDPs) as well as a major flow of conflict-affected persons towards neighbouring countries, requiring life-saving support. The overall unpredictability of the situation requires humanitarian actors to respond to the needs of the most vulnerable displaced and other conflict-affected communities &#x2013; and particularly female-headed households, children, persons with disabilities and/or chronic illnesses, as well as the elderly. Through this project, IOM aims at providing multi-sectoral assistance in those countries affected by the ongoing humanitarian situation, in line with the IOM Flash Appeal for the Ukraine Crisis, the OCHA-led Flash appeal for Ukraine and the Regional Refugee Response Plan for the Ukraine situation, published in March 2022.</narrative>
  </description>
